@startuml possession-flow-rebound
' ⚠ A DETAIL DIAGRAM. The whole possession, and the second-chance LOOP that
' wraps this one, are in possession-flow.puml — read that first.
' ⚠ THIS FILE OWNS: the rebounding foul (carved off the TOP), and the four-way
' missed-shot resolution. This is where MOST second chances are created.
' ⚠ ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING: the rebounding foul is rolled BEFORE the board
' contest and SHORT-CIRCUITS it — the whistle stopped play, so nobody rebounds.
' ⚠ Notes say what the flow DOES; the argument lives in possession-flow-model.md.
' Render: plantuml -DPLANTUML_LIMIT_SIZE=16384 -tpng   (every diagram is now under
'   the 4096px default, so the flag is insurance — but keep using it, and ⚠ keep each
'   diagram SCREEN-SIZED: past ~2,000px it stops being readable long before it stops
'   rendering. ⚠ `-checkonly` does not lay out and does not catch deprecated syntax
'   that renders as a warning box — look at the PNG.)
title Rebounding foul + MissedShotResolver\n//§3.8 the OOB carve · §3.10 rebounding fouls + bonus · §3.21 the rebound pool//

skinparam ActivityDiamondFontSize 11
skinparam ActivityFontSize 12
skinparam NoteFontSize 10

start
if (**rebounding foul?**\n//rareEventProbability, own base + sensitivity//\n//× defensivePressure — floor-free//) then (yes)
  note right
     **Carved off the TOP of the rebound phase** — rolled BEFORE
    the board contest and SHORT-CIRCUITING it on a hit (the
    whistle stopped play, so nobody rebounds). This keeps the
    rate independently tunable; it never entangles with the
    rebound weights.
     **TWO-SIDED**: a defensive box-out push (dominant) or an
    offensive over-the-back (the minority). The committer is
    drawn //foulProne//-weighted from the committing five.
  end note
  :FOUL — REBOUNDING
  committingTeamId = the committing side
  //opponentPlayerId is **NULL BY CONTRACT** — the foul is//
  //against the TEAM contesting the board; no individual victim//;
  if (committed by the DEFENSE?) then (yes)
    if (offense in the bonus?) then (yes)
      :FREE_THROW ×**2** — BONUS
      //shooter is a foulDrawing-weighted draw//;
    else (no)
    endif
    :→ **OFFENSE RETAINS** → second chance
    //back to the loop in possession-flow.puml//;
    stop
  else (no — committed by the OFFENSE)
    :→ **ball flips** → possession over
    //one of only two sites where the committer is on OFFENSE//;
    stop
  endif
else (no)
endif

:pick offensive rebounder (offenseRebound draw)
pick defensive rebounder (defenseRebound draw);

switch (**missed-shot outcome — ONE skill-weighted draw**\n//rebound balance: offenseRebound vs defenseRebound//\n//× fatigueFactor; OOB slices carved by a defense-leaning lean//)
case (OFFENSIVE rebound)
  :REBOUND — OFFENSIVE
  credit the off rebounder
  //this player becomes the putback candidate//
  → **OFFENSE RETAINS** → second chance;
  stop
case (DEFENSIVE rebound)
  :REBOUND — DEFENSIVE
  credit the def rebounder
  → **possession over**;
  stop
case (OOB — offense)
  :OUT_OF_BOUNDS_OFFENSE
  //credits NO rebounder — stays out of the reconciliation//
  → **OFFENSE RETAINS** → second chance;
  stop
case (OOB — defense)
  :OUT_OF_BOUNDS_DEFENSE
  //credits NO rebounder//
  → **possession over**;
  stop
endswitch

legend bottom left
  ONE draw, FOUR outcomes — the OOB slices are carved off the
  top by a flat defense-leaning lean FIRST, then the board contest
  runs on the clean-rebound remainder. NOT a separate "is it OOB?"
  sub-decision, so OOB never inherits the board winner.
  ⚠ Once the retention cap is reached, an offense-retained outcome
  is FORCED to a DEFENSIVE rebound — that is what bounds the loop.
  ⚠ THREE different offensive shares feed ONE rebound pool, and
  only one has a knob: the ordinary board contest
  (`base-offensive-rebound`), the block recovery (FIXED flat
  weights), and the free-throw board (a rule). Do NOT reach for
  `base-offensive-rebound` to move the other two.
endlegend
@enduml
